  "query_preview": "..FOR EXTREME SOUTHWESTERN CALIFORNIA INCLUDING ORANGE...\nSAN DIEGO...WESTERN RIVERSIDE AND SOUTHWESTERN SAN BERNARDINO\nCOUNTIES...\n\nA building strong high pressure today will center itself over \nsouthern NV and northern AZ this weekend. Easterly flow aloft will \nallow for periods of offshore winds through the weekend, especially \nin San Diego County. This will amplify already hot and dry \nconditions in the coastal basin. Model guidance suggests 500 mb \nheights will peak around 590 dm and 850 mb temps will reach 24-25 \nCelsius over the weekend. With offshore flow in place, this \ntranslates to surface temperatures well over 100 degrees through \ninland areas of the coastal basin Friday through Sunday. For western \nvalleys, highs will locally reach 105 or higher, especially in San \nDiego County on Saturday and Sunday. This will combine with lows in \nthe upper 60s to low 70s to create major HeatRisk throughout the \ncoastal basin from Friday onward. Areas of extreme HeatRisk expected \nfor coastal areas and western valleys.\n\nEasterly flow of 10-20 kts at 700 mb through the weekend will \nsupport weak Santa Ana winds gusting 25-45 mph (locally higher) \nalong west-facing slopes, adjacent foothills and locally into the \ninland valleys. The orientation of winds will favor San Diego County \nand downwind of the Banning Pass. Offshore winds in combination with \nheat and afternoon RH values of 15-25% will create elevated fire \nweather conditions for inland valleys and mountains through the \nweekend.\n\nOutside of the coastal basin, heat will be less anomalous. High \ntemperatures will range from the 70s in the mountains to near 100 in \nthe low deserts, which is only about 5-10 degrees above normal. \nThus, HeatRisk is minor outside of moderate risk in the low deserts.\n\nHeading into early next week, the mean of model guidance backs off \nsomewhat with the heat in the coastal basin as the high pressure \nweakens a touch and slides east. This will likely reduce or remove \noffshore wind potential for Monday and Tuesday. However, high \ntemperatures in the 90s to near 100 inland from the coastline will \nkeep major HeatRisk in place for most of the coastal basin. By mid \nto late next week, the general consensus is that upper ridging will \nstrengthen slightly again, keeping this heatwave firmly in place.",
